#!/bin/bash
# Refuse to commit while the tree is de-integrated.
#
# scripts/reset_to_clean.sh reverts every integrated unit's Fortran to the clean
# pin so `vit extract` has pristine source; scripts/restore_integrated.sh puts
# HEAD back. The pair is MANUAL and nothing guarantees the second runs, so a
# session killed, timed out, or simply ended in between leaves the tree
# reverted. That window opened twice on 2026-08-13.
#
# Committing inside it is the one irreversible outcome: a `git add -A` would
# record 28 units of de-integration as a real commit. Both occurrences missed
# that by timing alone, and the commit-each-artifact prompt rule multiplied the
# chances. This converts the irreversible half into a loud, self-explaining stop.
#
# THE COPY UNDER scripts/hooks/ IS THE SOURCE; .git/hooks/pre-commit is an
# INSTALLED copy. git does not version .git/hooks and `git bundle` does not
# carry it, so for its first five weeks this guard existed on exactly one
# disk, in no backup and no remote -- a guard whose own loss would be silent.
# Install or re-install with: bash scripts/hooks/install.sh
# Check for drift with:       bash scripts/hooks/install.sh --check
S="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.loop-run/TREE_IS_DE_INTEGRATED"
if [ -f "$S" ]; then
cat >&2 <<MSG

COMMIT REFUSED -- this tree is DE-INTEGRATED.

$(cat "$S")

Every integrated unit's C++ bridge is currently absent from
rosco/controller/src. Committing now would record that as the state of the
campaign.

  FIX:  bash scripts/restore_integrated.sh
        then commit again.

That is a checkout from HEAD; it restores the wrappers and clears this block.
Anything uncommitted under rosco/controller/src is lost by it, which is the
in-flight-integration case the script's own header warns about -- if you have an
integration you have not committed, re-run \`vit integrate ... --apply\` after
restoring and discard any gate result taken since.

Bypass with --no-verify only if you have read the above and mean it.

MSG
exit 1
fi

# Refuse to commit while a mutation sweep is unaccounted for.
#
# scripts/mutate_guarded.sh raises this and takes it down only when the
# translation hashes back to what it was before the sweep. Three of three hard
# kills left a mutant in the .cpp; the last was four characters and would have
# been rebuilt into libdiscon.so by the next restore. Committing one records a
# mutant as the translation -- the same irreversible half as the block above.
S="$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)/.loop-run/MUTATE_IN_PROGRESS"
if [ -f "$S" ]; then
cat >&2 <<MSG

COMMIT REFUSED -- a mutation sweep is unaccounted for.

$(cat "$S")

Either a sweep is running right now -- in which case the translation on disk is
a MUTANT and anything measured against it is measuring the mutant -- or one was
killed and never restored the file.

  FIX:  check the hash above. If it disagrees:
            git checkout HEAD -- <the file named above>
        then remove .loop-run/MUTATE_IN_PROGRESS and commit again.

Bypass with --no-verify only if you have read the above and mean it.

MSG
exit 1
fi
exit 0
